kbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[303,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[321,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[299,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[314,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1607,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1819,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[968,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[580,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[583,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[579,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[581,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[582,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[584,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1367,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[378,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[411,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[899,"`Enter/Space`"],[453,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[674,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[420,"`Escape`"],[856,"`Escape`"],[901,"`Escape`"],[1612,"`Escape`"],[480,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1929,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[588,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1887,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[504,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[662,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[691,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1802,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1857,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[720,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1856,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[755,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[381,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[851,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[847,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[967,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1659,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1314,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1602,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[682,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[665,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[893,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[668,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[927,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[932,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1041,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1821,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1822,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1820,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[858,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[903,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[424,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[587,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[586,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[347,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[997,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1051,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1176,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1050,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1175,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1564,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1563,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[761,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1484,"`size` is the tier: the eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`,\nand the body on `body`. Use `2xl` for a page title, `xl` for a hero, `lg` for a section\ntitle, and `md` (the default) everywhere else."],[503,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name."],[1855,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[46,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1393,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[969,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[44,"`Tab`"],[422,"`Tab`"],[451,"`Tab`"],[676,"`Tab`"],[854,"`Tab`"],[1610,"`Tab`"],[1318,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1315,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1319,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1317,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1428,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1489,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1108,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[800,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1601,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[1813,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[801,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[1823,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[1801,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1661,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1806,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1797,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1858,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1799,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or w